WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:03.109
- I'm so sorry I can't hug.

00:00:03.109 --> 00:00:04.501
I get in trouble.

00:00:04.501 --> 00:00:05.709
(audience cheers)

00:00:05.709 --> 00:00:07.140
We're getting closer to hugs.

00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:08.412
I feel it.

00:00:08.412 --> 00:00:09.245
I feel as though we're
getting closer to hugs.

00:00:09.245 --> 00:00:10.078
Maybe not.

00:00:10.078 --> 00:00:10.911
I don't know.

00:00:10.911 --> 00:00:11.744
Can he sit there?

00:00:11.744 --> 00:00:14.730
No. Yes? Yep. Nope. Yep.

00:00:14.730 --> 00:00:15.780
- I'll come here.

00:00:15.780 --> 00:00:16.650
Sorry.

00:00:16.650 --> 00:00:18.071
- You can sit closer.

00:00:18.071 --> 00:00:19.589
- Wow.

00:00:19.589 --> 00:00:21.917
- I'll go to this one.

00:00:21.917 --> 00:00:22.750
- [Stage Crew] Same one.

00:00:22.750 --> 00:00:23.583
- Same one?

00:00:23.583 --> 00:00:24.694
That's where I went the first time.

00:00:24.694 --> 00:00:25.527
- Oh my God.

00:00:25.527 --> 00:00:26.360
Did y'all know that we were going to play,

00:00:26.360 --> 00:00:28.380
what's that game we
played in the chair game.

00:00:28.380 --> 00:00:29.294
- Musical chairs!

00:00:29.294 --> 00:00:30.127
- Musical chairs.

00:00:30.127 --> 00:00:31.170
You didn't know, but
that's what's happening.

00:00:31.170 --> 00:00:33.203
- [Jenny] They didn't tell us.

00:00:33.203 --> 00:00:34.036
- I have a Goldilocks thing I like to do.

00:00:34.036 --> 00:00:36.120
Just test every chair when I come out.

00:00:36.120 --> 00:00:37.560
- You're like Goldilocks.

00:00:37.560 --> 00:00:39.462
You're checking them out. (laughs)

00:00:39.462 --> 00:00:40.539
- Yeah. Which bed's softest?

00:00:40.539 --> 00:00:41.372
- I love it.

00:00:41.372 --> 00:00:42.780
- You'll just fall asleep.

00:00:42.780 --> 00:00:43.780
Yeah, take a snooze.

00:00:44.940 --> 00:00:46.354
- I wish I could be one

00:00:46.354 --> 00:00:47.187
of those people that
falls asleep anywhere.

00:00:47.187 --> 00:00:48.020
Can you do that?

00:00:48.020 --> 00:00:49.050
- Now, I can.

00:00:49.050 --> 00:00:50.100
- [Kelly] Well, yes, now you can.

00:00:50.100 --> 00:00:51.367
You're a mom!

00:00:51.367 --> 00:00:52.200
Congratulations. Yeah! (audience claps)

00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:53.604
- Thank you.

00:00:53.604 --> 00:00:54.437
- And congratulations, you
just got married, right?

00:00:54.437 --> 00:00:55.723
- I did, I did.

00:00:55.723 --> 00:00:58.230
I just got married about a month ago.

00:00:58.230 --> 00:01:01.429
- Oh my gosh. Congratulations.
(audience claps)

00:01:01.429 --> 00:01:02.780
That's so cool.

00:01:02.780 --> 00:01:04.680
So what is it like,
married life at your house?

00:01:04.680 --> 00:01:05.513
You like it so far?

00:01:05.513 --> 00:01:06.690
- I like it.

00:01:06.690 --> 00:01:07.620
I like it.

00:01:07.620 --> 00:01:08.550
I'm a born romantic.

00:01:08.550 --> 00:01:10.980
I'm very suited to it, I think.

00:01:10.980 --> 00:01:12.270
Yeah, we got married,

00:01:12.270 --> 00:01:14.220
we got married on New Year's Eve,

00:01:14.220 --> 00:01:15.053
which is a nice.

00:01:15.053 --> 00:01:16.170
- [Kelly] That's beautiful.

00:01:16.170 --> 00:01:17.520
- Oh, thank you.

00:01:17.520 --> 00:01:18.600
- [Kelly] Beautiful, yeah.

00:01:18.600 --> 00:01:21.090
- It was my husband's great-grandmother's.

00:01:21.090 --> 00:01:22.470
- I was going to say, oh, I love that.

00:01:22.470 --> 00:01:23.520
I was like, there's a story there.

00:01:23.520 --> 00:01:24.570
That's so beautiful.

00:01:24.570 --> 00:01:27.990
- There is. There's a story stere.

00:01:27.990 --> 00:01:30.060
- No I just meant, more
than like it's just

00:01:30.060 --> 00:01:30.960
a brand new ring he bought.

00:01:30.960 --> 00:01:32.400
It looked like beautiful and antique.

00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:33.598
- I know.

00:01:33.598 --> 00:01:34.431
And now I'm kind of like

00:01:34.431 --> 00:01:36.731
I think there's some
banana bread batter also.

00:01:38.670 --> 00:01:39.907
It is the kind thing where they're like,

00:01:39.907 --> 00:01:40.740
"Will you marry me?"

00:01:40.740 --> 00:01:41.573
And you're like, "Yes.

00:01:41.573 --> 00:01:43.380
Are you sure you want to give me that?"

00:01:44.340 --> 00:01:46.101
- I'm going to ruin this.

00:01:46.101 --> 00:01:47.430
- Because you've met me before

00:01:47.430 --> 00:01:48.300
and I have the back

00:01:48.300 --> 00:01:49.500
of my dress tucked into my underwear.

00:01:49.500 --> 00:01:51.350
You know what I mean?

00:01:51.350 --> 00:01:52.200
- That's my kind of person.

00:01:52.200 --> 00:01:53.940
Wait, so did you get
married at your house?

00:01:53.940 --> 00:01:54.773
- Yes.

00:01:54.773 --> 00:01:58.020
- Wait, so was that stressful or exciting?

00:01:58.020 --> 00:02:00.510
- My best friend told me that
I was surprisingly chill,

00:02:00.510 --> 00:02:02.280
which I will brag about on national TV.

00:02:02.280 --> 00:02:03.862
- You should.

00:02:03.862 --> 00:02:05.348
Most people don't, aren't that way.

00:02:05.348 --> 00:02:06.330
- Yeah. Yeah. Yeah. I was chill about it.

00:02:06.330 --> 00:02:07.860
We only had 23 people.

00:02:07.860 --> 00:02:10.810
It was like after many cancellations

00:02:11.690 --> 00:02:12.523
and we actually, I mean,

00:02:12.523 --> 00:02:14.749
now it just seems like I'm weird,

00:02:14.749 --> 00:02:18.960
but we live in my husband's
great-grandmother's house, too.

00:02:18.960 --> 00:02:20.130
- Oh my gosh.

00:02:20.130 --> 00:02:21.000
I love this.

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:22.650
Everything is you're going to become her.

00:02:22.650 --> 00:02:25.816
- I know. I'm just like, wave goodbye.

00:02:25.816 --> 00:02:26.791
- Wait, I heard about this though,

00:02:26.791 --> 00:02:27.624
because the house,

00:02:27.624 --> 00:02:28.980
she used to throw like huge
parties or whatever, right?

00:02:28.980 --> 00:02:30.210
Do people have weird dreams?

00:02:30.210 --> 00:02:31.043
Did I hear?

00:02:31.043 --> 00:02:32.186
- Yes.

00:02:32.186 --> 00:02:33.019
- Okay. Okay, what?

00:02:33.019 --> 00:02:34.162
- That's what they say.

00:02:34.162 --> 00:02:35.400
I mean, my dreams are all weird,

00:02:35.400 --> 00:02:36.233
so I'm like I don't know.

00:02:36.233 --> 00:02:39.390
It seems normal to me, but yeah.

00:02:39.390 --> 00:02:41.700
- Definitely his
great-grandmother haunting you.

00:02:41.700 --> 00:02:43.140
- [Jenny] Oh for sure. Yeah.

00:02:43.140 --> 00:02:45.095
- Give me my ring back!

00:02:45.095 --> 00:02:45.928
(audience laughs)

00:02:45.928 --> 00:02:47.553
- Get that banana bread out.

00:02:49.274 --> 00:02:50.898
- She's got my ring!

00:02:50.898 --> 00:02:54.030
- I heard, did she throw
like crazy fun parties?

00:02:54.030 --> 00:02:55.860
- She threw crazy parties there.

00:02:55.860 --> 00:02:57.660
Their family calls it the Playhouse.

00:02:57.660 --> 00:03:00.213
It's like where they would dance.

00:03:01.996 --> 00:03:03.210
And apparently, like throughout the years,

00:03:03.210 --> 00:03:05.550
guests who, they come, they stay

00:03:05.550 --> 00:03:06.660
and they wake up and they're like,

00:03:06.660 --> 00:03:09.150
I had some crazy dreams last night.

00:03:09.150 --> 00:03:10.260
- [Kelly] Oh, some crazy good ones?

00:03:10.260 --> 00:03:11.727
- Yeah. Crazy party dreams.

00:03:11.727 --> 00:03:12.750
- When can I come over?

00:03:12.750 --> 00:03:13.750
- Any time you want.

